00:40:03.810 --> 00:40:05.480
What we're doing is we're--

00:40:05.480 --> 00:40:08.570
if you're using our Apigee
Edge micro gateway today,

00:40:08.570 --> 00:40:09.750
it's very similar.

00:40:09.750 --> 00:40:12.721
We're essentially charging
based on the number of API calls

00:40:12.721 --> 00:40:13.720
that are coming through.

00:40:13.720 --> 00:40:15.261
So typically, you
have an entitlement

00:40:15.261 --> 00:40:18.870
of several hundred
million calls per quarter

00:40:18.870 --> 00:40:21.950
or several hundred
million calls per--

00:40:21.950 --> 00:40:23.510
billion calls per year--

00:40:23.510 --> 00:40:25.261
sorry, tens of billions
of calls per year.

00:40:25.261 --> 00:40:27.093
And so what we're doing
is we're essentially

00:40:27.093 --> 00:40:29.030
calculating those API
calls that are coming

00:40:29.030 --> 00:40:31.730
in through the adapter
for Istio at a 3 to 1

00:40:31.730 --> 00:40:37.020
ratio, similar to what we
do for the micro gateway.

